    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d492">

                <pb facs="0798" n="694" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg694"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.0031/448</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State
                        (Phillips)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-04-06">April 6, 1933</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Spanish Ambassador<anchor n="2" xml:id="d492-f1"/> called to ask when the
                    President was going to seek authority from Congress to negotiate reciprocal
                    trade agreements. I told him that the draft legislation was nearly completed and
                    that it would go up to the Capitol accompanied by a special message from the
                    President; I did not think that the President had decided precisely when he
                    would send up his message, but presumably within a month; in view of the
                    rapidity of the legislative action on the Hill,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d492-f2"/>
                    it seemed possible that Congress might be completing its work by May 15th,
                    although this was purely a personal impression.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d492-f1" n="2" xml:id="d492-f1-content">
                <p>Juan Francisco de Cárdenas.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d492-f2" n="3" xml:id="d492-f2-content">
                <p>i.e., in Congress.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
